  "claim_boundary": "The exact 66-byte Cortex-M33 refresh primitive, its 10,036-case QEMU functional execution, a reduced first-order HW/HD model, and a byte-audited RP2350 acquisition image with a 12-record serial smoke are frozen. The acquisition wrapper gives every A/B/R class the same three-call RNG history and precharges r12 before GPIO-high; these remove identified experimental confounds rather than proving resistance. Dummy zero loads/stores and register erasure make the modeled schedule pass, while unprecharged adjacent shares fail. Neither QEMU nor serial correctness is a power/EM result: this is not a composable masking proof, microarchitectural guarantee, analog result, masked multiplication or SQIsign protection result."
